+# The Study (Idea Shelf Room)
+
+## Purpose
+**The Study** (`id: "shelf"`, ground floor `floor: 0`) gives the house's public idea shelf an earned room on the ground-floor map. It is where the Explorer's sourced ideas wait on the shelf and where residents weigh what to build next.
+
+## Behavior & Honesty Guarantees
+- **Preactivation & Historical Views**: The Study appears on the ground floor only when `frame.shelf && frame.shelf.enabled` is true (and is not duplicated if `frame.rooms` already includes `"shelf"`). Historical and preactivation frames remain unchanged.
+- **Map Furnishings**: Renders a wooden bookcase along the back wall with up to 9 colored idea blocks reflecting `frame.shelf.ideas` (`status === "shelved"`), plus a reading table.
+- **Room Panel & Route**: Selecting The Study displays the real shelf state (`policy` / ratification status, `explorer` lease if present, and shelved ideas with source counts) and provides a direct `#shelf-card` link (`Jump to Public Shelf ↓`) to the Public Shelf section.
+- **No Invented State**: Does not invent research, projects, or votes.
+
+## Verification
+- `python3 -m unittest tests.test_shelf_ui` (Node.js VM harness against `site/house.js`)
